le; in this subtest, token/window outputs satisfy the test'\"'s \"'`expect(..., 1e-3)` comparison and window/token outputs match bytewise (`:405`, `:449-455`). |\n| 5. `src/kernels/cpu/expert_multi_test.cpp` | **Selected.** Canonical expert identity/token-row arithmetic: four different synthetic blobs; multi-token and row-sliced execution must equal the matching single-token expert output bytewise (`:56-65`, `:78-109`). | **Yes, ISA-conditional.** No files/model/GPU. Requires AVX-512/VNNI/VBMI capability and OS support; exits 77 when `cpu_features().usable()` is false (`:49-52`). | CPU CMake `expert_multi_test` -> `strata_kernels_cpu`; skip code 77 (`CMakeLists.txt:2741-2744`). Canonical path works with `STRATA_NATIVE_EXPERTS=OFF` (native stubs: `src/kernels/cpu/expert_layout.cpp:422-432`). | Exit 0 with every token bitwise equal for each expert and n=1..MAXT, including row path. Run **without `--bench`** (`:78-110`). Exit 77 is reported separately. No dispatch adapter, router weights or changing-layer activation cache is exercised. |\n| 6. `tests/core/gguf_geometry_test.cpp` | **Selected.** Model/kernel compatibility refusal: missing keys, invalid top-k, contradictory attention/SSM keys, compiled-shape mismatch, RMS epsilon and wrong architecture (`:181-266`). | **Yes.** Generates tiny GGUFs in `TMPDIR`; no pre-existing model or GPU. Do not pass optional `--real`. | CPU CMake `gguf_geometry_test` -> header-only `strata_artifact` (`CMakeLists.txt:325-331`, `:364-366`). | All explicit checks pass, exit 0 and `all passed` (`:281-282`). Refusal messages must name the offending keys/architecture. Does not call the legacy host expert callback with bad width. |\n| 7. `tests/core/model_family_test.cpp` | **Selected.** Family/geometry/layout compatibility: architecture and engine guards (`:199-217`), family metadata (`:222-258`), full tensor layouts accepted; wrong shape, missing tensor and foreign-family tensor rejected (`:261-288`). | **Yes.** Synthetic temporary GGUFs; no external model/GPU. Do not pass optional `--real` (`:190-191`). | CPU CMake `model_family_test` -> `strata_artifact` (`CMakeLists.txt:355-358`). | All explicit checks pass, exit 0 / `ALL PASSED` (`:290-291`). This protects artifact family/layout identity, not runtime routed expert IDs. |\n| 8. `tests/prefill/routed_stream_test.cpp` | **Selected.** Production header'\"'s routed issuer/gate: each routed entry reads its own ring bytes, only published unrouted entries dropped, ring/depth bounds (\"'`:175-195`); real host-thread interleavings preserve bookkeeping/identity (`:203-280`). | **Yes.** Simulated copies and synthetic routes; no files/model/GPU. Uses host threads, not CUDA streams. | CPU CMake `routed_stream_test`, include path + `Threads::Threads` (`CMakeLists.txt:401-406`; Threads resolved at `:2042`). | Exit 0 / `OK`; checks fixed cases, 38 randomized simulations, six threaded walks (`:338-409`). This is issuer/consumer ordering, not the `HitFn` dispatch sequence. |\n\n## Protection gaps under this CPU-only gate\n\n- **Direct expert-cache mapping/residency:** no CPU-only protection found for the actual `ExpertCache` admission/allocation path. The exchange test verifies the separate host ownership mechanism; it cannot substitute for candidate 1'\"'s CUDA-backed cache assertions.\n- **Authoritative router/top-k and once-only weighting:** no runnable CPU-only production-router or Qwen pool-to-\"'`moe_combine` integration test found. The GPU candidates demonstrate relevant assertions, but extracting their host references or passing a device-unavailable skip would not validate the production path. The no-double-weight contract is at `include/strata/core/expert_source.hpp:15-17`.\n- **Stale activation at a stable address / stale hit rows:** no direct CPU-only adapter regression found that overwrites the same `x_f` buffer across calls, alternates hit/miss rows, and checks fresh reference outputs. Production explicitly requantizes each call (`src/core/expert_source.cpp:4745-4747`), clears previous hit rows (`:5373-5377`), and forbids previous-layer `mixed` quantization reuse (`:5385-5393`). The selected expert arithmetic test quantizes its inputs before the comparisons; it does not exercise this adapter contract.\n- **Current expert identity and `hit_hook` dispatch ordering:** host ownership/ring identity checks above are narrower than current-layer adapter IDs. The required sequence is `Launch -> pool -> H2D misses -> Combine -> post`, with current IDs provided to `Launch` (`include/strata/core/hit_hook.hpp:13-21`, `:30-39`; `src/core/expert_source.cpp:4749-4756`). No direct CPU-only regression for that sequence was found. CMake conditionally names `bench/micro/hit_cpu_order_parity.cu` (`CMakeLists.txt:2718-2720`), but that source is **absent at this checkout**; it is not an available test, and its declared build is CUDA-only anyway.\n\n## Offline build feasibility\n\nThe selected subset has an offline route without modifying Strata. Top-level GPU options support OFF (`CMakeLists.txt:80-94`, `:431`); the runner also disables SYCL, gfx906 and split-engine paths. Crucially, **native experts default ON** (`:176`): leaving that default would enter `FetchContent_Populate` for llama.cpp when `STRATA_GGML_DIR` is empty (`:2050-2057`, `:2104-2116`). Set `STRATA_NATIVE_EXPERTS=OFF`; the five selected tests need neither downloaded ggml nor Catch2. The local `third_party/ggml` contains format support files, not a complete llama.cpp `ggml` CMake project, and `third_party/llama.cpp` is absent. Do not assume a vendored full dependency checkout.\n\n`tests/CMakeLists.txt` is absent here. Its optional `add_subdirectory` is existence-guarded (`CMakeLists.txt:2887-2892`), so no extra suite or Catch2 is configured through it. Set `STRATA_BUILD_TESTS=ON` explicitly: the default depends on that absent file (`:162-171`). `FETCHCONTENT_FULLY_DISCONNECTED=ON` and Docker `--network none` add defense; disabling the fetch'\"'s feature gate is the actual dependency solution. No package install, submodule update, download, copied source tree, patch, or source-local generated file is needed by this recipe. Successful compilation remains unverified under the assignment's no-build restriction.\nEOF\ncat > builds/strata-tests/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Strata CPU mechanism tests (T-G)\n\nThis recipe selects \"'`exchange_storage_test`, `routed_stream_test`, `expert_multi_test`, `gguf_geometry_test`, and `model_family_test` at Strata commit `ffa80d73133ea5c548aefe57889a16e8085a938f`. See [select.md](select.md) for the eight-candidate table, source evidence and coverage limits.\n\n**Status: statically inspected; shell and embedded Python syntax checked. Docker, CMake configure, compilation and tests were not run.**\n\n## Exact invocation\n\nRun on the Docker host. The image must already exist locally; this command cannot pull it. Use an empty `container-build` directory for the first run (the script is mounted separately).\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /home/muk/projects/siminfeng/campaign/builds/strata-tests/container-build\ndocker run --rm --pull=never '\"\\\\\n  --label campaign=c1 \\\\\n  --cpus 8 --memory 16g --memory-swap 16g \\\\\n  --network none --read-only \\\\\n  --user \\\"\"'$(id -u):$(id -g)\" '\"\\\\\n  --env NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=void \\\\\n  --env CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES= \\\\\n  --mount type=bind,src=/home/muk/projects/Strata,dst=/src,readonly \\\\\n  --mount type=bind,src=/home/muk/projects/siminfeng/campaign/builds/strata-tests/container-build,dst=/build \\\\\n  --mount type=bind,src=/home/muk/projects/siminfeng/campaign/builds/strata-tests/run_cpu_tests.sh,dst=/runner.sh,readonly \\\\\n  --workdir /build \\\\\n  campaign/cuda-tools:c1 bash /runner.sh\n\"'```\n\nNo GPU is requested or exposed by the command. Use the ordinary Docker CPU runtime. The source and runner mounts are read-only; the container root is also read-only. All runner outputs, compiler scratch files, temporary synthetic fixtures and logs are directed under `/build`. Container `/build/results.json` becomes host `builds/strata-tests/container-build/results.json`.\n\nThe runner refuses an unverifiable or different source HEAD. The source checkout must include its readable Git metadata. Do not reuse a build directory configured for another source/generator; use a fresh empty directory instead. The host UID/GID must be able to write the build directory.\n\n## Build and execution behavior\n\nThe script configures the existing project with `cmake -S /src -B /build -G Ninja`, C++20 inherited from Strata, `Release` with `-O2 -UNDEBUG`, `STRATA_BUILD_TESTS=ON`, CUDA/HIP/SYCL/gfx906 OFF, and **`STRATA_NATIVE_EXPERTS=OFF`**. Other optional GPU/engine features are explicitly disabled. Both FetchContent disconnected switches are ON. The exact argument list is in [run_cpu_tests.sh](run_cpu_tests.sh).\n\nOnly four selected CMake targets are built, individually with `--parallel 8`; their required CPU library dependencies are built as needed. `exchange_storage_test` is compiled unchanged with standalone `g++ -std=c++20 -O2 -UNDEBUG -pthread -I/src/include ...`: its stock CMake declaration is inside the GPU gate although the implementation it tests is header-only. No Strata source is patched, stubbed or copied. Each successful build is followed by a direct executable invocation from `/build` with default arguments. No broad CTest run, benchmark mode, real-model mode or GPU rotation mode is used.\n\nThe runner attempts the standalone build even if CMake configuration fails. A build/test failure does not prevent later independent builds/tests. Configure timeout is 120 seconds, each build timeout 180 seconds, and each test timeout 60 seconds; timeout kills the process group. Tool-version/revision probes each have a 15-second timeout. Normal runtime is **estimated at 1–5 minutes** on an 8-CPU x86-64 host with local storage; this is unmeasured. The sum of the serial timeout budgets is about 24 minutes. Large logs/disk exhaustion or externally killed containers can prevent report completion.\n\n## Results and exit status\n\n`/build/results.json` contains `toolchain` entries for CMake, g++, Ninja, Git, Python, nvcc and `uname`, the source revision check, the complete configure command/result, and a `tests` array. Every test row contains the requested fields:\n\n- `test`: executable name; `built`: boolean for this build attempt.\n- `exit_code`: actual executable exit code, or `null` when it was not run. Negative values mean termination by a signal; runner timeout is 124.\n- `seconds`: build + run elapsed time for that test, excluding shared configuration; `run_seconds` is also recorded when run.\n- `stdout_tail`: final 8 KiB of combined stdout/stderr from the run, or the blocking build/configure log when not run.\n\nAdditional fields include `method`, `status`, `build_exit_code`, build/run commands, timings and log paths. Full logs live in `/build/logs/`. Results are saved atomically after each completed test, so prior results survive a later ordinary failure. The three excluded GPU candidates are documented in `select.md`; they are not built or mislabeled as passed in the JSON.\n\nRunner exit status: **0** = all five passed; **3** = all other tests passed but `expert_multi_test` skipped for missing CPU ISA (77); **1** = any build/configure/test failure; **2** = required source revision could not be verified. Missing optional nvcc metadata does not fail CPU tests; missing required CMake/compiler tools appears in the relevant build/configure results.\n\n## Known blockers and limits\n\n- `expert_multi_test` is CPU-only but needs AVX-512/VNNI/VBMI and enabled OS state. A host without them returns 77. Docker does not emulate missing instructions. Its canonical C++ kernel still compiles on the specified modern g++ toolchain; ISA flags are confined to kernel sources by Strata'\"'s CMake.\n- Native-expert support defaults ON and normally fetches llama.cpp. This offline recipe disables it. Enabling native tests without a separately supplied compatible full dependency checkout is not an offline recipe. No downloaded dependencies or model files are needed by the selected subset.\n- Direct GPU-cache residency/admission, authoritative top-k execution, and the related DeepSeek once-only combination oracle cannot run in this container without a GPU. The CPU ownership test only checks simulated aliases, and the routed-stream test only simulates device copies. No direct CPU test was found for stable-address stale activation reuse, current-layer hit IDs, or \"'`Launch/pool/H2D/Combine` adapter ordering.\n- CMake target availability and dependencies were inspected at the pinned source. Actual configure/build success and test verdicts must be established by running the command above; this assignment explicitly forbade doing so during preparation.\nEOF\nbash -n builds/strata-tests/run_cpu_tests.sh\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport ast\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('builds/strata-tests/run_cpu_tests.sh')\ns=p.read_text()\nembedded=s.split(\\\"exec python3 - <<'PY'\\\\n\\\",1)[1].rsplit('\\\\nPY\\\\n',1)[0]\nast.parse(embedded, filename=str(p)+':embedded-python')\nprint('bash -n: PASS; embedded Python ast.parse: PASS (runner not executed)')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
